  "notes": "{屈|かが}む describes bending the upper body forward or downward — stooping, crouching, or hunching.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{屈|かが}める→屈める：28924_kagameru⟧ (transitive: to bend something)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{屈|かが}んでいる means being in a stooped or crouched position.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{腰|こし}→腰：02210_koshi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{屈|かが}める: to bend at the waist (uses transitive form)\n- ⟦{身|み}→身：01764_mi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{屈|かが}める: to stoop, to duck\n- ⟦{前|まえ}→前：02255_mae⟧{屈|かが}み: bending forward (noun)\n- ⟦{背中|せなか}→背中：00810_senaka⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{屈|かが}んでいる: having a hunched back\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦しゃがむ→しゃがむ：05535_shagamu⟧: to squat, to crouch down (legs bend, body lowers)\n- {屈|かが}む: to stoop, to bend (upper body bends forward)",
